Loads: fewer, larger disc reads, and a slow-frame log

- open_track_at_cd_pos keeps the track's file open and only seeks: every
  CdRead went through it, closing and reopening the disc image with the
  audio lock held, a fopen on the Vita's SD card for each file the game
  loads (maps, menu images) while the audio thread waited.
- CdRead reads unbuffered, 128 sectors (300 KB) per fread: the Vita's
  newlib then reads straight into the chunk in one call, where through the
  64 KB stdio buffer a map change read the card at ~6 MB/s.
- PSYZ_GL_PERF (always on on the Vita): a frame of 100 ms or more logs a
  "hitch:" line with its disc reads (CdRead calls, sectors, ms), VRAM
  operations, HD image uploads and the rest ("other"); a run of frames over
  20 ms logs one "slow:" line when it ends, with how much of those frames
  went to the buffer swap ("swap", now timed apart from "present").

